    },
    "body": "The completed termination-weighted continuation does not meet its declared extension rule: three source completions improve beyond plain controls where four were required, and none of the20 sampled stories meets complete prose criteria. This records the implemented dose as INERT, preserves its modest gains and failures, and keeps the frozen Dot/Lorentz/Affine result as the next state/read decision.\n\nAdds a derived packet with actual parent/control/treatment output, generated IDs, stops, original file identities, row joins, guardrail values and recorded cost components. Updates current state and roadmap with the completed termination result, verified Claude pilot evidence and pending raw-artifact preservation; Dot/Lorentz fits are complete and Affine is running. The known weighted-shard defect limits interpretation to the objective actually run and does not trigger an automatic repair-fit.\n\nValidation: principal and independent prose/source review; original identities and extraction checked; claim-wording and relative-link checks; staged diff whitespace check. No Rust/runtime change, new fit, decoder sweep, model reload or full native seal revalidation. Resource components are distinguished from unresolved complete owning-lab accounting; overlapping elapsed is not charged twice.\n\nReferences #973. References #820.\n",
